    ":question/problem": "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}-11x+30.$\n\n${x}^{2}-11x+30=(x\\,\\,-$\n{{field-1}} $)^{2}-$\n{{field-2}}",
    ":question/worked-solution": "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+30\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}$, writing the constant term $30$ last:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{x}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}x+{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}}-\\,{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}^{2}+30\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last two terms, we get\n\n$$\n{(x-\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$"
  },
