    ":question/id": "7f9dddf9-bc9e-5a58-864b-3fea990dc262",
    ":question/problem": "Complete the square on $x^2-5x$.\n\nHalve the coefficient of $x$, then add and subtract the square of that half. Fill in the missing positive numbers.\n\n$x^2-5x=(x-$ {{field-1}} $)^2-$ {{field-2}}",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Write the linear term as $-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}x$. Add and subtract $\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2$ so the expression keeps its value:\n\n$$\nx^2-5x=\\underbrace{x^2-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}x+\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2.\n$$\n\nFactor the first three terms and evaluate the constant:\n\n$$\nx^2-5x=\\left(x-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe blanks are $\\frac{5}{2}$ and $\\frac{25}{4}$."
  },
