    ":question/id": "2b5c9b41-1c42-51fb-96be-bf1a1b427a01",
    ":question/problem": "Complete the square on $t^2-5t+7$. Choose the expression written as a perfect square plus a constant.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "The half of the linear coefficient is $-\\frac{5}{2}$. Add and subtract its square, keeping the original constant:\n\n$$\nt^2-5t+7=\\underbrace{t^2-2\\cdot\\frac{5}{2}t+\\frac{25}{4}}_{\\text{perfect square}}-\\frac{25}{4}+7.\n$$\n\nFactor the perfect square and combine the constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nt^2-5t+7&=\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2-\\frac{25}{4}+\\frac{28}{4}\\\\\n&=\\left(t-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2+\\frac{3}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minus sign inside the square gives the required linear term $-5t$; the remaining constant is positive."
  },
